// How an agent appraises the significant events of its life. Each event has two
// kinds of effect:
//   traits  PERSISTENT shifts to innate disposition (opposed traits move the other
//           way automatically — raising vengeance lowers forgiveness).
//   moods   TRANSIENT spikes to current feeling, which then fade (see moods.ron) —
//           and a sustained feeling, in turn, slowly reshapes the matching trait.
// This is an agent's *values*: author them freely.
[
    // Tasting power feeds ambition for good, and brings a flush of joy.
    (event: "Crowned", traits: [("ambition", 0.05)], moods: [("joy", 0.7)]),
    // Being cast down stirs hot anger; left to smoulder, anger is what — over a
    // life of being wronged — hardens into a lasting grudge (anger shapes vengeance).
    (event: "Deposed", moods: [("anger", 0.9)]),
    // Crossing a line you knew was forbidden hardens you to it: the first taboo
    // broken makes the next come easier (vengeance up, and so forgiveness down).
    (event: "Transgressed", traits: [("vengeance", 0.05)]),
]
